# companion: a check-in child's loadout. A fork copies its parent's, which
# carries the writable shell. A check-in only observes, so clear the copy and
# grant the read-only shell alone. Its report is its last message: the next
# tick reads that and writes the handoff note, so the child needs no write path.
# To let a check-in use another tool, add a line here (docs/companion.md).
set -e
kj binding reset
kj binding allow "facade:shell"
